### Start a call: opens a ringing call to peerUserId and returns the caller's join token.
# {{token}} is a Sanctum bearer token (POST /api/auth/login returns one).
POST {{host}}/api/voice/calls
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "peerUserId": 2
}

### Poll: the signed-in user's open call, if any (no token). The callee polls this every
### few seconds; a ringing call with role = callee is an incoming call. No data = no call.
GET {{host}}/api/voice/calls/current
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Accept (callee only): marks the call active and returns the callee's join token.
POST {{host}}/api/voice/calls/{{callId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Decline (callee only, while ringing): closes the room so the caller is dropped.
POST {{host}}/api/voice/calls/{{callId}}/decline
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Hang up (either side): cancels a ringing call or ends an active one; closes the room.
POST {{host}}/api/voice/calls/{{callId}}/hangup
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Rejoin token: a fresh join token for an open call you are part of.
POST {{host}}/api/voice/calls/{{callId}}/token
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### History: your most recent calls in both roles, newest first.
GET {{host}}/api/voice/calls?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
